        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-05T21:58:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for explaining it.\n\nI saw your latest patch makes the colors in the child-binding. You can add the `period` to the child-binding too. Each color has its `period`. So you don\u0027t need this `on_sec`. The `period` in the child-binding is not required for a solid color (LID_OFF is a solid color).",
      "parentUuid": "baead6e6_de575d23",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "12cd65e02f573309be2ebe31abc82e6b95c78efc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "06e86899_9271c644",
        "filename": "zephyr/dts/bindings/gpio_led/battery-led-colors.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 1513493
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-06T00:08:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I made period and on_sec optional. However, both the fields are necessary as the logic is\nif ((battery_ticks % period) \u003c on_sec)\n    color_1\nelse\n    color_2\n    \nIf period is moved in color_1 and color_2, then first we will have to check if color_2 exist, then get period from color_1 (period_color_1) and from color_2 (period_color_2) and do\n\nif ((battery_ticks % (period_color_1 + period_color_2)) \u003c period_color_1)\n     color_1\nelse\n     color_2\n    \nwhich I think increases the complexity, your thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "ff1b677f_c2dddb01",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "12cd65e02f573309be2ebe31abc82e6b95c78efc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
