      "writtenOn": "2021-10-06T18:29:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This global `period` and `on_sec` seem difficult to explain. The `on_sec` is not necessary a ON state, like the color-1 is LID_OFF. And how to support 3 colors?\n\nYou don\u0027t need to support variant length of colors. You can define a max length, like 4. You can store the nodes into an array, with the color and the accumulate the periods.\n\nFor example:\n\n\tcolor-1 {\n\t\tled-color \u003d \"LED_BLUE\";\n\t\tperiod \u003d 2;\n\t};\n\tcolor-2 {\n\t\tled-color \u003d \"LED_AMBER\";\n\t\tperiod \u003d 2;\n\t};\n\tcolor-3 {\n\t\tled-color \u003d \"LED_OFF\";\n\t\tperiod \u003d 3;\n\t};\n\n\nThe array looks like:\n\n\tstruct led_color_t led_colors[MAX_COLORS] \u003d {\n\t\t{\n\t\t .led_color \u003d LED_BLUE,\t\n\t\t .acc_period \u003d 2,\n\t\t },\n\t\t {\n\t\t .led_color \u003d LED_AMBER,\n\t\t .acc_period \u003d 4,\n\t\t },\n\t\t {\n\t\t .led_color \u003d LED_OFF,\n\t\t .acc_period \u003d 7,\n\t\t }\n\t\t {\n\t\t .led_color \u003d LED_OFF,\n\t\t .acc_period \u003d 7,\n\t\t }\n\t};\n\nThe code is to loop through the array to check the matched range.\n\n\tt \u003d battery_ticks % led_colors[MAX_COLORS - 1].acc_period\n\tfor (i \u003d 0; i \u003c MAX_COLOR; i++)\n\t\tif (t \u003c led_colors[i].acc_period)\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\tcolor \u003d led_colors[i].led_color;",
      "parentUuid": "06e86899_9271c644",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 26
      },
