      "writtenOn": "2021-10-06T00:08:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently led_values are a combination of current power_state which is set using charge_get_state() and chipset_state (if applicable). So each node represents a unique charge_state. \nled_values[PWR_STATE_COUNT][CHIPSET_STATE_COUNT]. \n\nAnd we lookup values using current power state\npwr_state \u003d charge_get_state();\n\ncolor_1 \u003d led_values[pwr_state][ANY].color_1;\n\nAdding an additional node makes the code more complex when chflags are only used in PWR_STATE_IDLE. This makes it more simpler:\n\nif (pwr_state \u003d\u003d PWR_STATE_IDLE) {\n    if (chflags \u0026 CHARGE_FLAG_FORCE_IDLE) {\n        /* color_1 x sec, color_2 y sec */\n    } else\n        /* color_3 */\n}\n\nSo I removed the chflags property in the latest patch. Do you agree?",
